      "fact": "The published node-start program is a template containing the PC3 address 192.168.45.222 twice (publish flag and PortBindings assertion). The PC2/PC4 receipts show 192.168.45.143/.210, so the bytes actually executed on PC2/PC4 differ from the published file and are neither published nor hashed. The recorded docker inspect results (asserted by the same program shape) bind the actual configuration.",
      "disposition": "Root should record the rendering rule (only that address literal substituted) and the SHA256 of each rendered PC2/PC4 program, or publish them. Non-blocking for observation acceptance."
    },
    {
      "id": "FT-L3",
      "severity": "LOW",
      "mandatory": false,
      "class": "conditional Root operational obligation (observer provenance)",
      "where": "pc3-actual-cpu-pilot-r1/pc3-standard-observer-image-r1/wheel-name-r2-receipt.json",
      "fact": "The observer runs /observer-bootstrap.py (SHA 8cccc5a1…) built by Dockerfile r2 (260f52d7…); neither file's bytes are public. Source inv.observer_worker.main reads INV_RUNTIME_DSN from the environment, so a bootstrap must read the secret file and enter the standard main. 'Standard observer, no custom poll loop' is therefore Root-attested; the reviewer can confirm only that the observed cadence and probe counts are consistent with the source loop.",
      "disposition": "Root should publish the bootstrap and Dockerfile r2 bytes (no secret content) or an AST summary pinned to those SHAs before treating the observer image as a reviewed standard deployment beyond this pilot."
    },
    {
      "id": "FT-L4",
      "severity": "LOW",
      "mandatory": false,
      "class": "conditional Root operational obligation (import provenance)",
      "where": "tools/fresh_cpu_admission.py:24 (1efea, SHA 8129ab5a…) as copied to the operator ops directory",
      "fact": "The CLI inserts Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]/'services/control-plane/src' at sys.path[0]. For the copied ops/fresh_cpu_admission.py that is <share>/services/control-plane/src on the PC3 operator host. The wrapper verifies the venv site-packages library SHA, not the module the CLI actually imports; that is the same module only if that share path is absent. The recomputed digests and 1efea-only APPLY receipt fields (readbackVerifiedBeforeCommit, nodeControlSeedVersion) are consistent with the verified library, so no contradiction exists.",
      "disposition": "Before further CLI use, Root should record read-only absence of <share>/services/control-plane/src (or invoke the library via a pinned entry that adds no path). No product change required for this acceptance."
